      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Oliver,\n\nThanks for the pointer. I looked at 93509 (patch set 8), and I don\u0027t think\nit covers the same thing as this change:\n\n- 93509 changes /redfish/v1/Chassis/{ChassisId}/Drives/{DriveId}. It moves\n  the chassis -\u003e drive lookup to the \"containing\" association and reworks\n  the drive property unpacking. Links/Chassis on that resource already\n  comes from the chassisId in the URL, so it was never wrong.\n\n- This change (95055) fixes\n  /redfish/v1/Systems/{SystemId}/Storage/1/Drives/{DriveId}. There,\n  Links/Chassis comes from getMainChassisId() and always points to the\n  first chassis in inventory. On Yosemite5, ssd0 is on\n  Yosemite5_Storage_Expansion_Board but the link says BMC_Storage_Module.\n  This is the reverse direction: drive -\u003e chassis through \"contained_by\".",
